  </main_text><notes>The left and right parts of the page are cut off, so some names end mid-word (e.g. "Auderifius, A", "Audilus, Aud", "Baldo, Baldu", "Baldieriu" cut); these are left as visible. The initial "B" of "Baldierius" and "Adicho" is a large initial and was read as a letter joined to its word. The last line "MmM" is a partly visible signature-like mark, read as printed. The column "Adicho" is set with a large B initial. Only the right-hand marginal notes are visible on this fragment; the main text column is not shown in this part of the scan, so no running text is transcribed. The notes are short names set in the margin and are copied as far as legible: "Iuderiffius." (upper, partly cut at left, first letter lost), "ilius." (partly cut), "Arilianus.", and further single-word notes ending in "s." or "us." down the margin, too faint or cut to read reliably. The foot line reads "{...} 3 Bera" with the first letters cut away. Page number 837 is printed at top right.</notes></page>
